// Distributed schedule: 4 compute workers row-band partition the
// outer `i` axis of the matmul triple loop. Host runs load/save.
// M5 AC#4 capstone cell for example 07 (TASK-0297). The TASK-0301
// per-data axis-mapping filter (cycle 118) is what makes this
// schedule lower bit-identical: `b` is indexed [k][j] so the filter
// excludes `i` from `b`'s tile bounds → empty bounds → whole-array
// broadcast of `b`. `a` (indexed [i][k]) and `c` (indexed [i][j])
// both carry the per-worker `i_band` slice on their tiles.
//
// PRD §11 M5: "Examples 5–7 benefit measurably" from
// distributed/reuse. Examples 5 and 6 closed cycles 79c..116; this
// is the example-7 closure.
//
// Partition shape
// ---------------
// `loop i : partition=workers;` on the outer axis. N=16, 4 workers,
// exact-divisible into 4-row bands (0..4, 4..8, 8..12, 12..16). Each
// worker computes c[i_band][full j] using a[i_band][full k] and
// b[full k][full j].
//
// Why this is bit-identical with naive/blocked
// --------------------------------------------
// The k-accumulator semantics are unchanged under the i partition:
// each output c[i][j] is the SAME sum over k = 0..N regardless of
// which worker computes it. Workers are independent on i; no halo,
// no cross-worker carry, no reduction across i. Therefore the
// existing reference.bin oracle applies — no new reference is needed.
//
// Why sync transfers
// ------------------
// Sync-only schedule lowers on every tier-1 backend
// (pthreads-sync, mp-tcp-bufsync, pthreads-async, mp-tcp-event)
// without capability gaps. Async variants are out of scope for the
// closeout cycle.

schedule for "../prog.algo.nuc" {
    workers = { host, w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    place load_a on host;
    place load_b on host;
    place save_c on host;
    place madd   on { w0, w1, w2, w3 };

    // Row-band partition the outer i axis. N=16, 4 workers → 4 rows each.
    loop i : partition=workers;

    // All sync transfers. a is row-banded by i, b is whole-array
    // broadcast (not indexed by i), c is row-banded by i on gather.
    transfer a : sync;
    transfer b : sync;
    transfer c : sync;
}
